glint (1.2.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Replace the multi-colour glass icon with an orange crop-frame G, with
    matching small-size and symbolic variants.
  * Use warm orange for selection outlines, guides, handles, confirmation
    buttons, text editing bounds and focused pin borders.
  * Add the author's email to preferences, with mail and copy actions, and
    update the package maintainer and AppStream contact information.

 -- chenwu <geekchenwu@gmail.com>  Mon, 26 Oct 2026 19:20:00 +0800

glint (1.2.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Build a single-file installer that uses APT to install the bundled Debian
    package and its dependencies, including python3-gi-cairo.
  * Allow capture, annotation, copy and basic pinning immediately after a
    first install through the system screenshot portal.
  * Provide temporary, conflict-aware shortcuts until GNOME loads the native
    extension at the next normal login, then remove the temporary shortcuts.
  * Keep existing shortcuts and user-disabled extensions intact; test initial
    setup in a separate desktop where the native extension is not registered.
  * Copy clipboard image bytes before the Shell callback releases them, and
    raise capture windows only after their first frame is available.

 -- Glint <glint@chenwu.local>  Mon, 26 Oct 2026 18:15:00 +0800

glint (1.1.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Export clipboard textures as GdkTexture so other applications receive
    image/png, and claim the clipboard before closing the capture overlay.
  * Encode lossless screenshot tiles in parallel to avoid blocking the
    selection overlay on full-desktop PNG compression.
  * Center the top bar menu on the Glint indicator.
  * Add image transport and cross-application paste regression checks.

 -- Glint <glint@chenwu.local>  Mon, 26 Oct 2026 17:25:00 +0800

glint (1.1.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Snipaste-style selection frame: the whole area outside the selection
    resizes the nearest edge(s), and the frame stays adjustable after
    choosing a tool or drawing.
  * Arrow keys move the selection by one pixel; Ctrl+arrow pushes that edge
    out, Shift+arrow pulls it in. W A S D step the pointer one pixel.
  * R restores the last region, Space hides the toolbar, [ and ] change the
    pen size.
  * A press made before the editor is up no longer reaches the window under
    the frozen frame.

 -- Glint <glint@chenwu.local>  Mon, 26 Oct 2026 14:40:00 +0800

glint (1.0.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * First release: in-shell capture (F1 / Ctrl+F1) that keeps menus and
    popups in the shot, annotation editor, pins (F3 / Shift+F3),
    preferences, and first-run shortcut hand-over from Snipaste.

 -- Glint <glint@chenwu.local>  Mon, 26 Oct 2026 14:00:00 +0800
